From b9ca065485dd95e05d788e79321d0f537599ab81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yichao Yu <yyc1992@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 20:15:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 20/21] mma, ccsaq: Newton-type dual solver behind the
 "dual_newton" parameter

The dual problems of MMA and CCSAQ are solved by a general bound-constrained
optimizer (dual_algorithm, MMA by default), which uses only first
derivatives and takes hundreds to tens of thousands of dual function
evaluations per subproblem when there are many (nearly active) constraints.

With "dual_newton" = 1 (default 0, which leaves the results unchanged), the
dual problem is solved instead by a primal-dual interior point method with
Mehrotra's predictor-corrector, using the Hessian of the dual function,
B^T B with B = (G D^{1/2})^T: G is the Jacobian of the constraint
approximations at x(y) and D the inverse second derivative of the separable
Lagrangian in the components of x(y) not at a bound.  The new dual_hess
functions of mma.c and ccsa_quadratic.c compute B from the state left by
dual_func.  The Newton system is solved directly if there are fewer
multipliers than free variables, and otherwise through the smaller matrix
by the Woodbury identity, leaving out the negligible columns of the
inactive constraints.  An active-set (projected) Newton method was tried
first: it needs hundreds to thousands of iterations to identify the active
constraints when there are many nearly active ones.

dual_algorithm is still used for the subproblems of an infeasible start
(upper bounds of 1e40 on the multipliers) and for CCSAQ with a
preconditioner.  With an external BLAS/LAPACK, the Newton matrix is formed
with dsyrk and factorized with dpotrf (added to the configure check).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
